    "updated_at": "2026-10-09T12:16:10Z",
    "body": "**Decision:** The era boundary is the HistData stamp `2018-12-16 00:00` (`ERA_SWITCH` in `sources/histdata.py`). Stamps before it decode as `America/New_York`; stamps from it on decode as `Europe/Zurich` minus six hours.\n\n**Evidence:** HistData's SPXUSD tick file for 2018-12, fetched once for this check (2 requests, kept in scratch only, not in the repository):\n- From 2018-12-02 to 2018-12-14, 82–93% of each day's quotes have both bid and ask on the 0.25-point grid. From 2018-12-16 to the end of the month, 0% do.\n- The old feed's last tick is stamped `20181214 165959847` (Friday) and the new feed's first is `20181216 180007859` (Sunday). The switch falls in that weekend's market close.\n- The session shape changes at the same point. Friday's last tick moves from 16:59 to 16:14 (stamp time), and Sunday's first moves from 18:01 to 18:00.\n\n**Trade-off:** any boundary inside that weekend gives the same ticks. In December both rules give UTC−5 anyway: New York is on standard time, and Zurich standard time (UTC+1) minus six hours is also UTC−5. So the exact choice inside the close changes no output; only the side of the boundary a tick falls on matters.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
